Description: merge KiCad solder-paste gerbers into one stencil order
 Stencicrity takes the gerber exports of several KiCad projects and lays every
 board side out on a single stencil sheet, so that a batch of small boards can
 be ordered as one stencil instead of one stencil per project.
 .
 It copies all paste openings over, marks the border of every board with
 dotted lines so the sheet can be cut apart afterwards, and places dowel-pin
 holes on a fixed grid so that every cut-out piece fits the same fixture
 plate. The result is a single F_Paste gerber, packed in a zip together with a
 copper reference layer, that a stencil house cuts like any other.
 .
 Copper pads that have no paste opening in the source - test points, jumper
 pads, connectors soldered by hand - are collected and presented in a curses
 terminal interface, where each of them is either opened or left closed. The
 decisions are stored in a plain text file next to the gerbers, so a second
 run over the same boards needs no interaction.
